(PRC-38 — the environment is inherited from the calling process.
 HOME is set in any ordinary session; the exec'd shell sees it.
 Also hand-verified with the argv-dumping helper of PRC-34, which read
 environment's "PRC_MARKER" and printed the value the parent was started
 with, in all three Execute forms.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-38.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   the environment came through
)
Execute "/bin/sh" with arguments ["-c", "case $HOME in ?*) echo the environment came through;; esac"].
On error print "the exec failed".
